WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.536
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:17.399
Unit thirty-one: Sentential and Non-finite Relative Clauses. Today you will comment on a whole clause and reduce relative clauses.

4
00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:20.235
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.549
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:26.233
Which.

7
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.364
Which means refers back to a whole clause, after a comma.

8
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.240
The train was late, which annoyed us.

9
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.282
Your turn. Say: Which.

10
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:39.879
Which.

11
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.478
Whereby.

12
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:44.344
Whereby means by means of which.

13
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.449
A system whereby people share cars.

14
00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.540
Your turn. Say: Whereby.

15
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.471
Whereby.

16
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:55.997
Whence.

17
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:59.854
Whence means from which place, in formal writing.

18
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.974
The village whence he came.

19
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:04.887
Your turn. Say: Whence.

20
00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:08.676
Whence.

21
00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:10.975
Sentential relative.

22
00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:15.434
Sentential relative means a which-clause about a whole clause.

23
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.562
A sentential relative.

24
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.244
Your turn. Say: Sentential relative.

25
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.867
Sentential relative.

26
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:27.978
Non-finite.

27
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:31.633
Non-finite means without tense or subject.

28
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:33.984
A non-finite clause.

29
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:37.584
Your turn. Say: Non-finite.

30
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.609
Non-finite.

31
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.409
Reduced.

32
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.940
Reduced means shortened.

33
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:47.992
A reduced clause.

34
00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:50.702
Your turn. Say: Reduced.

35
00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:54.382
Reduced.

36
00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:56.338
Comment clause.

37
00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.139
Comment clause means a clause that gives an opinion.

38
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.355
A comment clause.

39
00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.591
Your turn. Say: Comment clause.

40
00:02:08.433 --> 00:02:09.864
Comment clause.

41
00:02:10.617 --> 00:02:12.071
Extra information.

42
00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:16.035
Extra information means non-essential details.

43
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.824
Extra information in commas.

44
00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:22.568
Your turn. Say: Extra information.

45
00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:27.166
Extra information.

46
00:02:27.967 --> 00:02:31.432
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:34.689
Visal, add a comment to The train was late.

48
00:02:35.783 --> 00:02:50.826
The train was late, which annoyed everyone. Here which refers to the whole situation, not to one noun. This is a sentential relative clause and it always follows a comma.

49
00:02:51.917 --> 00:02:53.916
What are non-finite relatives?

50
00:02:55.017 --> 00:03:09.038
They reduce a relative clause with a participle or infinitive: The students attending the class are tired. The first person to arrive was Tom. The plan agreed yesterday is final.

51
00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.964
What about whereby and whence?

52
00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:27.895
Whereby means by which and appears in laws and reports: a system whereby citizens vote online. Whence means from where and is literary. In everyday English, use by which and from where.

53
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.673
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:31.517 --> 00:03:39.310
Grammar focus: Sentential relative: main clause, which plus comment; non-finite: noun plus participle and infinitive.

55
00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:40.785
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:41.483 --> 00:03:43.843
The train was late, which annoyed everyone.

57
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.028
The students attending the class are tired.

58
00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:49.951
The first person to arrive was Tom.

59
00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:58.118
Use , which for a whole clause. Reduce relative clauses with -ing, -ed or to-infinitives. Whereby = by which.

60
00:03:58.883 --> 00:04:03.022
Be careful! Don't say: The train was late, what annoyed us.

61
00:04:04.967 --> 00:04:08.116
Say: The train was late, which annoyed us.

62
00:04:08.416 --> 00:04:09.602
Use which here.

63
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.890
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:14.864
Adding a Comment.

65
00:04:15.164 --> 00:04:17.790
The flight was cancelled, which annoyed everyone.

66
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.577
The students attending the lecture were very tired.

67
00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:25.054
The first person to arrive was the director.

68
00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:30.411
The council introduced a system whereby residents report problems online.

69
00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.584
Such clauses add comments and compress information.

70
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.667
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:40.517 --> 00:04:42.702
The train was late, blank annoyed us.

72
00:04:43.002 --> 00:04:46.249
A, which. B, that. C, what.

73
00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.602
The answer is A: which.

74
00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.877
The people blank the class are tired.

75
00:04:55.177 --> 00:04:59.040
A, attended. B, attending. C, attend.

76
00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:04.449
The answer is B: attending.

77
00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:07.815
The first person blank arrive was Tom.

78
00:05:08.115 --> 00:05:11.118
A, to. B, for. C, at.

79
00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:16.689
The answer is A: to.

80
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.350
Whereby means blank.

81
00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:23.397
A, at which. B, by which. C, from where.

82
00:05:26.933 --> 00:05:28.817
The answer is B: by which.

83
00:05:29.983 --> 00:05:33.330
According to the reading, what can residents report online?

84
00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.202
A, problems. B, taxes. C, weather.

85
00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:42.789
The answer is A: problems.

86
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.268
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:48.117 --> 00:05:52.034
Add a sentential 'which' clause to this sentence: 'The train was late.'

88
00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.583
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:02.883 --> 00:06:12.968
The train was late, which made me miss my first class. The train was late, which was frustrating for everyone. The word which refers to the whole situation.

90
00:06:13.268 --> 00:06:15.105
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:16.017 --> 00:06:25.786
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and sentential relative: main clause, which plus comment; non-finite: noun plus participle and infinitive.

92
00:06:26.086 --> 00:06:31.409
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:31.709 --> 00:06:34.663
See you in Unit thirty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:34.963 --> 00:06:38.555
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

